it because it is not defined at $x=0$ (it makes zero the denominator).   Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval  $[0,1)$   is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-2,-1]$    is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-2,-1].$   Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73487/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73487"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129216/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "6dbfc494-6449-5563-b282-e70c7261f2f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129216/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "db1068bb-24e9-5090-abd3-30e6b24cee6b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129216/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "9e7cba34-02c2-5a3c-89ed-ec78b4a26097" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129216/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "1e3a46ab-d7c3-561a-a574-035f9f3cb201" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129216/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "909188b9-d538-5721-bfe5-5d5591c64413" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129216/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd050d78-7eef-5cd7-bdff-bbe56a81d378" :answer-field